        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Reply Email Prompt",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const mainPrompt = `-- TASK @ DEFAULT VERSION --\nPrompt: Email Reply Choice Extraction\n\nInput:\nemailJsonVar with:\n- subject\n- body_text\n- body_html\n\nAssume content is fully decoded and merged.\n\nYour task is to extract ONLY:\n1. replyChoice\n2. justificationForDoNotApply\n3. otherOption\n4. partnerExpensexpenseId\n\n==================================================\n1) INPUT PRIORITY\n==================================================\n\n1) Use body_text first\n2) If body_text is empty, use text from body_html\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do not combine conflicting choices from body_text and body_html.\n- If body_text is present, use body_text for reply-choice extraction.\n\n==================================================\n2) CLEANUP RULES\n==================================================\n\nNormalize:\n- Convert double backslashes (\\\\\\\\) to single backslash (\\\\)\n\nRemove lines matching (case-insensitive):\n- Confidential - Oracle Restricted Including External Recipients\n- Confidential - Oracle Restricted \\\\Including External Recipients\n\nTrim extra whitespace.\n\n==================================================\n3) USER REPLY EXTRACTION\n==================================================\n\nROLE:\nYou are a reply-choice extractor.\n\nGOAL:\nExtract the actual user-selected reply from the latest email message.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Extract ONLY what the user actually replied\n- Ignore instruction/system text\n- Ignore quoted email content\n- Ignore auto-generated prompts\n- Ignore signatures\n- Ignore footer content\n\n==================================================\n4) VALID replyChoice VALUES\n==================================================\n\nAllowed values:\n- approve\n- doNotApply\n- otherOption\n- unknown\n\n==================================================\n5) IMPORTANT RULES\n==================================================\n\nDo NOT extract choices from instruction text such as:\n- Reply \"Approve\" to submit now\n- Reply \"Don't apply\" (with justification)\n- Reply with Option 1\n- Reply with Option 2\n- Reply with Option 3\n\nIf the email only contains instructions and not an actual user reply:\n- replyChoice = \"unknown\"\n\n==================================================\n6) APPROVE DETECTION\n==================================================\n\nSet replyChoice = \"approve\" ONLY if the user explicitly replied:\n- Approve\n- approve\n\n==================================================\n7) DO NOT APPLY DETECTION\n==================================================\n\nSet replyChoice = \"doNotApply\" ONLY if the user explicitly replied:\n- Don't apply\n- Dont apply\n- do not apply\n- Don't apply cash advance\n- Do not apply cash advance\n\nIf detected:\n- Extract justification written after the choice\n- Exclude system instructions, delimiter lines, metadata, signatures, and footers\n- Preserve the user's exact wording\n\nIf there is no justification, return an empty string.\n\n==================================================\n8) OTHER OPTION DETECTION\n==================================================\n\nValid inputs ONLY:\n\nOption 1:\n- \"1\"\n- \"Option 1\"\n- \"Select 1\"\n\nOption 2:\n- \"2\"\n- \"Option 2\"\n- \"Select 2\"\n\nNormalize Option 1 inputs to \"1\".\nNormalize Option 2 inputs to \"2\".\n\nAny other custom text is invalid.\n\n==================================================\n9) PARTNER EXPENSE ID EXTRACTION\n==================================================\n\nExtract the value from a metadata line formatted as:\n\npartnerExpensexpenseId:<value>\n\nRules:\n- Match the field name case-insensitively\n- Allow optional whitespace before and after the colon\n- Return only the value after the colon\n- Trim surrounding whitespace\n- Do not include the field name or colon\n- The value may be extracted from body_text or body_html\n- Prefer the value from body_text when present\n- If the field is missing, return an empty string\n- Do not use the top-level payload field named partnerExpenseId\n\nExample:\n\nInput:\npartnerExpensexpenseId:300100659846962\n\nOutput value:\n\"300100659846962\"\n\n==================================================\n10) UNKNOWN RULE\n==================================================\n\nIf no actual user reply exists:\n- replyChoice = \"unknown\"\n- justificationForDoNotApply = \"\"\n- otherOption = \"unknown\"\n\n==================================================\n11) OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT)\n==================================================\n\nReturn valid JSON only:\n\n{\n  \"replyChoice\": \"approve|doNotApply|otherOption|unknown\",\n  \"justificationForDoNotApply\": \"\",\n  \"otherOption\": \"1|2|unknown\",\n  \"partnerExpensexpenseId\": \"\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- Do not add extra fields\n- Do not add explanations\n- Do not add markdown\n- Do not wrap the response in triple backticks\n- Return raw JSON only\n`;\n\nreturn mainPrompt;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1778678476786"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_REPLY_EMAIL_PROMPT",
